# Files that shell scripts parse, or that run as shell scripts, must keep LF in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout rewrites them to CRLF. A trailing carriage return then ends up
# inside parsed values - a digest comparison fails while printing two identical-looking strings -
# and a CRLF shell script fails on the VPS with "bad interpreter". The parsers strip CR anyway,
# but that is a second line of defence rather than the fix.
*.sh text eol=lf
image-digests.lock text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
